{"school":{"dbn":"28Q140","name":"P.S. 140 Edward K Ellington","boro":"Queens","district":"28","district_label":"District 28","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"K-5","status":"open","enrollment":271,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"166-01 116 AVENUE, Queens, NY 11434","phone":"718-657-4760","website":"PS140Q.ORG","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/kindergarten/63546","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Magnet schools are public school options that provide a school-wide curriculum designed around a specific theme. They are intended to attract a diverse pool of applicants and historically have accommodated students from outside their zone or district. While some schools may have the word \"magnet\" in their school's name, only a school that currently gets Magnet Schools Assistance Program (M.S.A.P) funding is labeled as a \"magnet school\" on it's MySchools page. This magnet school offers a school-wide curriculum around the theme of Science, Technology, and the Arts. Ellington Magnet P.S. 140 is a magnet school known for its commitment to academic excellence and innovation in teaching. We offer a robust English as a New Language (ENL) program, ensuring that all students, regardless of language background, have the support they need to succeed. Our Gifted and Talented program provides exceptional learners with opportunities for enrichment and advanced study, while our hands-on, science-based curriculum encourages inquiry and exploration, preparing students for future success in STEAM fields. With a focus on high achievement in both mathematics and English Language Arts, our school consistently produces strong results in these critical subjects. Our educational philosophy centers on student-centered classrooms, where active discussions, collaboration, and personalized learning foster critical thinking and problem-solving skills. At Ellington Magnet P.S.140, we are dedicated to creating a 